 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? I usually shop with a backpack on my back, so I can reach the top shelf. Do you have a pannier or basket? A basket is great for shops with low ceilings, since you can tip it right onto the floor. Most towns have a bike shop that rents them. Then you can do one big shop a week and carry it all in one go. Plan what you need each day and carry only that. It can be. A backpack that's too big or too heavy shifts your center of gravity, which can be trip hazard.",
